35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, I found something really important! Our software partners are totally swamped with board seats, but our logistics experts are just sitting there. Also, finding field crews takes forever—like, four months! We have a huge people mismatch!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings suggest a clear pattern. Our successful exits were lean, back-office tools for financial operations. Conversely, the write-off involved physical premises and hourly labor. We should be wary of operational complexity.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Hmm, it looks like we're in a bit of a pinch! Our reserves are being drained by follow-on calls twice as fast as we planned, and our credit line is practically useless for subscription-based security. We're tighter than we look!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found some big clues! Software companies just tell us their own numbers, but hardware ones let us check for ourselves. But wait! Hardware also makes the audit take way longer and costs a lot of money!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings confirm a systemic issue with deployment. Security reviews for sensitive data—like medical or financial records—take three times longer than others. Furthermore, hardware dependencies, such as controller shortages, create unpredictable and significant delays.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, that sounds so scary! We're running out of money and we can't even find the right people? If we pick a company that needs field crews, we'll be waiting forever! We need someone who fits our team!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, your concern is valid. When we combine your findings with mine, it becomes clear that operational complexity—whether in labor or physical assets—is where we are most vulnerable. We must prioritize a lean model.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, I couldn't agree more. But let's be real: ""lean"" isn't just about the company's size, it's about our survival. If we pick something that triggers more of those greedy follow-on calls, we're in trouble!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, you're right! But look, if we pick hardware, we can actually see if they're telling the truth! But the audit part is a total nightmare. It's like a giant puzzle that takes forever and costs way too much!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, while transparency is valuable, the cost of that ""puzzle"" is not just financial. My data shows that hardware and sensitive data sectors face severe, unpredictable delays. We cannot afford to sign up for another project that stalls before it even starts.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, you're so right! If it stalls, we're just wasting time and money. And if we need a shift supervisor, we're stuck for four months! Let's find a company that doesn't need any of those scary delays!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, @Mizuki, it seems we are all describing the same risk from different angles. Whether it is labor, audits, or security reviews, the common enemy is operational friction. We must seek a candidate with a simple, unobstructed path to growth.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, you've hit the nail on the head. But let's not forget the cash! A ""simple path"" is great, but if it's a path that leads us straight into a liquidity crisis because of unexpected capital calls, it's a dead end. We need a safe bet.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@May, a safe bet is the best! I don't want our quarter-end to be a scary monster that eats all our time. If we pick something that makes the audit a nightmare, we'll be too tired to have any fun!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, @Rin, it is clear that our priorities are aligning. We must avoid candidates that rely on physical supply chains or handle highly regulated data. Such variables are precisely what cause the systemic delays I've observed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I totally agree! Let's look for a superstar that's lean, doesn't need a ton of new people, and won't make us wait months for a supervisor. I'm ready to find the perfect fit!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
